.example/v2/` (with a trailing `/v2/`), while the new code was also updated to append `/v2/charges` to the base URL. This resulted in double-slashed and duplicated path segments (`/v2//v2/charges`), which the payment gateway rejected with a `404 Not Found` error.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n- **Logs**:\\n  `ERROR payments-api: paygate request failed: 404 Not Found url=https://api.paygate.example/v2//v2/charges`\\n- **Recent Changes**:\\n  `PAYGATE_URL: https://api.paygate.example -> https://api.paygate.example/v2/ ; client now calls {PAYGATE_URL}/v2/charges`\\n\\n## Remediation\\nRoll back the deployment of `payments-api` to the previous stable version (`payments-2.14.x`) and restore the original `PAYGATE_URL` configuration.\\n\\n## Follow-ups\\n1. Fix the URL construction logic in `payments-api` to safely join paths without duplicating segments.\\n2. Synchronize the system clock on the `payments-api` hosts to resolve the ~15-minute clock skew observed in the logs.\"\n}\n```", "output_ref": null, "tool_calls": [], "output_tokens": 929, "latency_ms": 18469, "input_tokens": 21069, "cached": true, "provider": "gemini"}
